  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "observed_first_failure",
      "finding": "All three first validation failures are pi-pre-allow: actual HTTP200 deny/block/native_command_control_authority_block instead of allow. Two pre receipts in each report were admitted and equal full SQLite readback."
    },
    {
      "kind": "source_fixture_precondition",
      "finding": "The reused _start_installed_daemon creates fresh GuardStore without prepare_empty_command_authority. Existing generated production-key qualification fixture and default-auto probe explicitly require protected empty authority for a synthetic command allow corpus. Rust global_block is true for nonprotected health or a global-lockdown layer; reports do not retain which exact state selected it."
    },
    {
      "kind": "source_observer_schema_mismatch",
      "finding": "PiReceipts requires receipt rule_digest equal compact current_snapshot_binding rule_digest. Product compact binding deliberately omits rule_digest. Both actual pre rows have null observed ACK rule and valid nonnull receipt rule; this independently prevents observer completion. Bind receipt rule to admitted installed capability/manifest and preserve generation/policy/runtime joins to compact ACK; do not invent an ACK field."
    },
    {
      "kind": "source_product_limit_consistent_with_observation",
      "finding": "All three actual source callbacks per cell send guard_payload_ref and raw-native entry sees matching ciphertext digest; native review returns without a valid receipt and availability response says native_post_tool_unavailable. Exact edge payload_kind classifies this as encrypted before source ref, and evaluate_validated_envelope unconditionally rejects encrypted references. Python raw edge forwards the payload without hydration. The retained artifact does not identify the erased Rust leaf or exclude an earlier transport/admission failure for an individual call."
    }
  ],
